# N2/STO-3G FCIQMC -- the first validation on a system where sampling is real.
#
# 10 orbitals, 7 alpha / 7 beta, ndet = 14400. This is the research scope's
# primary fixture: FCI is affordable (~8 s at 4 threads) so the gate has an exact
# reference, AND the determinant space is large enough that a few-thousand-walker
# population is a genuine SAMPLE rather than covering the space.
#
#   RHF          -106.7665937606
#   exact FCI    -107.6529998854   (correlation fci on this input)
#
# Every earlier FCIQMC gate ran either on a synthetic Hamiltonian or on H2/STO-3G,
# whose 4 determinants are far below where sampling means anything. This is the
# first case that tests the method rather than the plumbing.
#
# PARAMETER CHOICES, and why:
#
#   fciqmc_walkers 10000    0.7 walkers per determinant. Deliberately BELOW
#                           saturation -- F4.4 and F4.5 both found that a
#                           saturated space stops exhibiting the sampling
#                           behaviour being validated. At 200000 (13.9/det) this
#                           would cover the space and prove nothing.
#
#   fciqmc_timestep 0.001   Conservative. F4.3 put the controlled-dynamics
#                           boundary at 0.26-0.30x the diagonal bound, and the
#                           diagonal bound is itself 2.28x larger than the true
#                           spectral one. A diverging population is a hard error
#                           naming the timestep, not a wrong number.
#
#   zeta 0.3 / xi 0.05      Inside the band F4.1 measured. The usable band is
#                           system-specific (the gain is zeta/(interval*dt)), so
#                           these are a starting point, not a tuned optimum.
#
#   granularity 1.0         One walker. Without discretization the propagator is
#                           scale-invariant and the noise does not depend on
#                           population at all (F4.4).
#
#   initiator 0.0           OFF. The initiator is a biased approximation; this
#                           gate validates the method against an exact answer, so
#                           it must not be hidden behind one.
#
#   seed 20250901           Fixed, and echoed in the output. A rerun with the
#                           same seed must reproduce the trajectory bitwise.

%begin_control
    basis       sto-3g
    calculation energy
    verbosity   normal
    basis_type  cartesian
%end_control

%begin_scf
    scf_type    rhf
    correlation fciqmc
    ci_max_dim  200000

    fciqmc_walkers         10000
    fciqmc_timestep        0.001
    fciqmc_shift_damping   0.3
    fciqmc_shift_restoring 0.05
    fciqmc_shift_interval  5
    fciqmc_granularity     1.0
    fciqmc_initiator       0.0
    fciqmc_equilibration   2000
    fciqmc_steps           8000
    fciqmc_spawn_attempts  1
    fciqmc_seed            20250901

    use_diis    .true.
    diis_dim    8
    save_checkpoint .false.
    engine      os
    guess       hcore
%end_scf

%begin_geom
    coord_type  cartesian
    coord_units angstrom
    use_symm    .false.
%end_geom

%begin_coords
2
0   1
N     0.000000     0.000000     0.000000
N     0.000000     0.000000     1.098000
%end_coords
